# Stub environment for the browser e2e suite (e2e-browser/).
#
# EVERY VALUE IN THIS FILE IS FAKE. These exist only to satisfy the
# hard-required tier of lib/env.ts (Supabase, OpenAI, Clerk) so `next dev`
# boots for the Playwright webServer. Never put real credentials here —
# this file is committed.
#
# - Supabase points at the local stub PostgREST server started by
#   playwright.config.ts (e2e-browser/stub-supabase.mjs). It serves a single
#   seeded Space ("e2e-demo") and empty results for everything else, so
#   server-rendered public pages (/apply/[slug], /status) are deterministic.
# - The Clerk publishable key is a syntactically valid pk_test_* key whose
#   base64 payload decodes to "clerk.example.com$" — enough for @clerk/nextjs
#   to boot without entering keyless mode. No session cookie is ever present,
#   so clerkMiddleware treats every request as signed-out without any network
#   call. Tests block all non-localhost requests anyway.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:55321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=e2e-stub-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=e2e-stub-service-role-key
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-e2e-stub-not-a-real-key
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_e2e_stub_not_a_real_key
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_Y2xlcmsuZXhhbXBsZS5jb20k
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3100
